Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 the encounter swirl covers the 16:9 picture

FIELDSTG_playBattleTransition copies the 320 x 240 display to VRAM (MoveImage
to x 0x280) and breaks the copy into 5 x 6 tiles that slide off in a spiral.
The side gutters are not in VRAM, so the swirl was a 4:3 copy: the gutters
went black on its first frame and the tiles slid off inside the 4:3 box (0051
only widened the darkening quad).

With widescreen on (gutter > 0; off, the code is the PS1's): the copy is taken
from the buffer on display (GFX.disp[GFX.dispBuffer]), the last frame drawn;
the buffer at y 0 can be the one drawn next, whose gutters the renderer has
already blanked at the flip. Right after the MoveImage,
dw3_port_widescreen_copy_gutters (PSY-Z Psyz_VideoCopyGutters) puts
the gutter columns of the same rows beside the copy in VRAM, left of x 0x280
and right of x 0x280 + 320. Each row then gets two more tiles, one of gutter
width hanging off the left edge of the row's first tile and one off the right
edge of its last tile, sampling those strips. They take the position of the
tile they hang off, and drop out when it does, so the spiral keeps its order
and its frame count. 0051's widened darkening quad is unchanged.

